💡 **SUGGESTION: `parseMcpPrList` duplicated verbatim across both helper files**

This PR adds the identical function to `js/postMobileTestAutomationResultsHelpers.js:160` and `js/preCliMobileTestAutomationSetupHelpers.js:282`:

```js
function parseMcpPrList(parsed) {
    if (Array.isArray(parsed)) return parsed;
    return (parsed && parsed.data) ? parsed.data : [];
}
```

`parseMcpDataList` is likewise a near-twin (non-array branch only). The repo already has a shared home for MCP response-shape parsing in `js/common/smProvider.js` (`parseMcp` + `asList`, dependency-free at module level), and `js/common/` is the designated shared-helper layer per AGENTS.md.

The per-module self-containment follows the established gh-1034/gh-979 helper-file pattern, so this is not blocking — but a follow-up could hoist `parseMcpPrList`/`parseMcpDataList` into a small `js/common/mcpResult.js` and have both helper files re-export, preventing the three copies from drifting apart.
